these actors played their child roles so  convincingly that we never had any idea  they were  actually grown-ups join us as we explore  the history of adults who played kids in  movies and fooled us all  in the 2002 romantic comedy bend it like  beckham parmender nagra stars as a  london teen named jess who joins a local  women's soccer team  at the urging of her friends her natural  talent for the sport shines through and  jess is soon leading the team on its way  to the championship  in the movie jess becomes close friends  with her teammate jules played by keira  knightley  and a budding romance develops between  jess and her young and attractive coach  joe not everything is perfect though as  the championship takes place on the same  day as jess's sister's wedding  and jess's strict parents have forbidden  her to play and don't even know she's on  the team  although bend it like beckham is just a  sports themed spin on the traditional  teen romcom the star of the movie wasn't  even close to being a teenager herself  when nagra played 18 year old jess in  the film the actress was actually 26.  casting directors frequently age up when  picking actors to fill roles in team  movies and amy heckerling's 1995  coming of age comedy clueless is a  pretty classic example of this  in fact most of the main clueless cast  members were slightly older than the  characters they played in the movie  at the start of the film cher played by  alicia silverstone  is 15 years old while silverstone  herself was 17 at the time  similarly josh played by paul rudd is a  college undergraduate student while rudd  was 25 during filming  however the one clueless star that  really fooled audiences was stacy dash  who played cher's best friend  dion if you've seen clueless you might  have assumed dash was around the same  age as her on-screen classmates  in fact the actress was actually 28 when  she played the 16 year old dion  what's more dash went on to reprise her  role in 62 episodes of the clueless  television series spin-off  from 1996 to 1999. while the teens do  grow  older during the course of the show that  still left dash then in her  early 30s playing an 18 year old when  the series drew to a close  in 2004 the small indie comedy napoleon  dynamite took the world by storm  this quirky cult classic takes a look at  the awkward and awesome adventures of  high school student napoleon dynamite  played by john heater  as he navigates life in small town idaho  alongside his friend pedro who was  played by efren ramirez  filmed on a budget of just 400 000  napoleon dynamite earned over 46 million  dollars at the box office and turned  heater and ramirez  into celebrities almost overnight  that's a pretty good idea heater could  probably still pass for a high school  student today  so it may not surprise you to learn that  the babyfaced actor and producer was  actually 26 while working on napoleon  dynamite  what we really want to know is how  ramirez keeps his youthful good looks  though  not only was he nearly 30 during filming  but the mustache he grew for the part  actually made pedro look even younger  than he was supposed to be  in the classic 1987 romance dirty  dancing recent high school graduate  francis baby houseman spends a summer  with her affluent family at a resort in  the catskill mountains where she meets  dance instructor johnny castle played by  patrick swayze after baby agrees to fill  in for johnny's dance partner penny at  an upcoming performance  she and johnny grow closer as they  practice together and help penny out of  a tough situation  she may have been playing a fresh-faced  17 year old but gray was no baby when  she appeared in dirty dancing  although she definitely looked like a  typical american teenager the actress  was actually 27 years old which would  become one of her most widely remembered  roles  in fact in 2020 it was announced that  gray would be reprising her  unforgettable role in a sequel to the  original movie  even if you've never read a single one  of jk rowling's wildly popular harry  potter books you're likely familiar with  the minor character moaning myrtle  though you might not have known her name  myrtle is one of the many ghosts that  haunt hogwarts school of witchcraft and  wizardry and her first big screen  appearance came during 2002's harry  potter and the chamber of secrets  in that film harry ron and hermione  learn more about myrtle and how she died  during some uncomfortable encounters in  the bathroom she likes to haunt  her exact age isn't specified in the  harry potter movies or books but context  clues suggest she was killed when she  was around 13 or 14 years old  looks like mining myrtles flooded the  bathroom believe it or not scottish  actress shirley henderson was actually  37 when she first appeared as the  distressed ghost in 2002's chamber of  secrets  this makes her by far the oldest actor  to portray a hogwarts student on screen  ghosts don't age of course so henderson  later beat her own record when she  reprised the role of myrtle in 2005's  harry potter and the goblet of fire at  age 39.  in the 1996 comedy the bird cage robin  williams stars as  armond goldman an openly gay man who  owns a drag queen club  in south beach near the start of the  film armond learns that his son val  played by dan futterman is in love with  18 year old barbara keely played by ally  mcbeal favorite kalista flockhart the  only problem is barbara is the daughter  of a prominent florida senator and she  worries about how her conservative  parents will react if they learn the  truth about armand's lifestyle  as a result armond agrees to pretend to  be straight when the keeley's come for a  visit  even arranging for val's mother to  pretend to be his wife  as you might expect things don't work  out quite according to plan  although calista flockhart and the rest  of the birdcage cast were mostly a  backdrop for the comedic talent of the  late robin williams 